    {
      "id": "kqgzrtj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.1 Location & Extent"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Chhattisgarh is divided into four primary physiographic divisions: Northern Hills, Chhattisgarh Plain, Dandakaranya, and Jashpur Plateau.",
        "The Chhattisgarh Plain is locally referred to as the Maidan, forming the central region of the state.",
        "Dandakaranya forms the southern hilly region of Chhattisgarh, while the Northern Hills constitute the northern plateau area.",
        "The chapter outlines essential geographical studies including Location & Extent, Rivers, Mountains & Peaks, Climate, and Districts."
      ],
      "id": "tcejlx1"
    },
